4.6 PARTIAL EXIT MAXIMUM QUANTITY

STATUS:

COMPLETE

Bug identified:

The Edit Trade UI previously calculated the maximum editable Partial Exit quantity using reconstructed Trade.quantity values.

This incorrectly treated the final remaining position as though it limited the selected exit.

Example:

100 BUY

20 SELL

20 SELL

20 SELL

20 SELL

20 remaining

Previous incorrect maximum:

20

Correct maximum for an individual exit while keeping all other executions unchanged:

40

The calculation was replaced with lifecycle-execution-based chronological analysis.

The new calculation:

* Collects lifecycle executions
* Deduplicates execution IDs
* Identifies the exact selected exit execution
* Orders executions deterministically
* Calculates position before the selected exit
* Evaluates all later lifecycle executions
* Determines the maximum replacement quantity that does not create an invalid negative position

This works for both LONG and SHORT semantics.

Important:

pairTrades was NOT modified.

FIFO was NOT modified.

The defect was correctly fixed at the Edit Trade UI validation layer.

Result:

COMPLETE

Priority:

HIGH

